  "header": {
    "id": "asset",
    "name": "Asset",
    "description": "Assets - each asset is an instance of an asset design, if the assets are serialized.\n\nIf assets are not serialized, you need only create 1 asset to represent the asset. Only Assets in Fuuz will track production usage (out of the box). You can use Asset Groups, to define an \"assembly\" of assets - like a mold/die - with assets being individual details or components that you want to track. If you only want to track the overall assembly (for usage) - just set it up as an asset (skip asset group).",
    "dataModelKindId": "reference"
  },
